{"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.038, 0.404, 0.948, 0.455], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For nonterminal states,  "}, {"type": "equation_inline", "content": "\\min_{s \\in States}(Utility(s,p)) <= Eval(s, p) <= \\max_{s \\in States}(Utility(s,p))"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.088, 0.475, 0.385, 0.518], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "i.e. Between a win and a loss"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.039, 0.545, 0.169, 0.588], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Must be fast"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.038, 0.616, 0.956, 0.664], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Common approach: Define features of the state, give each feature a weight, combine into a"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.038, 0.686, 0.647, 0.741], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "weighted linear function: "}, {"type": "equation_inline", "content": "w_1 * f_1(s) + w_2 * f_2(s) + \\ldots + w_n * f_n(s)"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.054, 0.923, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.108, 0.938, 0.286, 0.966], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 4, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.04, 0.113, 0.782, 0.178], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adversarial Search - Evaluation Functions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.26, 0.55, 0.301], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Example: In chess, suppose we use the following features:"}]}, {"type": "code", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.04, 0.308, 0.308, 0.351], "content": [{"type": "algorithm_body", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.04, 0.308, 0.308, 0.351], "content": [{"type": "equation_inline", "content": "f_{1}(s) = \\text{Number of white pawns}"}]}], "sub_type": "algorithm"}, {"type": "equation", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.04, 0.356, 0.308, 0.399], "content": "\\mathrm{f} _ {2} (\\mathrm{s}) = \\text {Number of black pawns}"}, {"type": "equation", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.04, 0.403, 0.318, 0.448], "content": "\\mathrm{f} _ {3} (\\mathrm{s}) = \\text {Number of white bishops}"}, {"type": "equation", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.041, 0.451, 0.318, 0.496], "content": "f _ {4} (s) = \\text {Number of black bishops}"}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.038, 0.592, 0.775, 0.641], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "With the following weights (for white's perspective): "}, {"type": "equation_inline", "content": "w_1 = 1"}, {"type": "text", "content": ", "}, {"type": "equation_inline", "content": "w_2 = -1"}, {"type": "text", "content": ", "}, {"type": "equation_inline", "content": "w_3 = 3"}, {"type": "text", "content": ", "}, {"type": "equation_inline", "content": "w_4 = -3"}, {"type": "text", "content": " ..."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.038, 0.688, 0.699, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "So our evaluation function is the weighted sum of all features times weights:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.04, 0.744, 0.23, 0.807], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Eval(s, p) = "}, {"type": "equation_inline", "content": "\\sum w_{i}^{*}f_{i}(s)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.039, 0.818, 0.609, 0.862], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "But don't forget to normalize between -1 and 1 (or min/max utility)"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.054, 0.923, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.108, 0.938, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 5, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.04, 0.113, 0.852, 0.182], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adversarial Search - Alpha-Beta cutoff search"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "code", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.037, 0.241, 0.999, 0.904], "content": [{"type": "code_body", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.037, 0.241, 0.999, 0.904], "content": "def alpha_beta_search(game, s): ...\n    def max_value_abc(game, s, alpha, beta, depth):\n        if game.Is-Cutoff(s, depth): return game.Eval(player, s), None\n        val = -infinity\n        for a in game.Actions(s):\n            v2, a2 = min_value_abc(game, game.Result(s, a), alpha, beta, depth+1)\n            if v2 > val:\n                val, move = v2, a\n                alpha = max(val, alpha)\n            if val >= beta: return val, move\n        return val, move\n\n    def min_value_abc(game, s, alpha, beta, depth):\n        if game.Is-Cutoff(s, depth): return game.Eval(player, s), None\n        val = infinity\n        for a in game.Actions(s):\n            v2, a2 = max_value_abc(game, game.Result(s, a), alpha, beta, depth+1)\n            if v2 < val:\n                val, move = v2, a\n                beta = min(val, beta)\n            if val <= alpha: return val, move\n        return val, move"}], "sub_type": "code", "guess_lang": "python"}, {"type": "footer", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.054, 0.924, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.109, 0.938, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 6, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.04, 0.112, 0.657, 0.177], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adversarial Search - Cutoff Search"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.26, 0.615, 0.308], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When should game.Is-Cutoff(s, depth) return True?"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.038, 0.332, 0.538, 0.378], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When depth == limit, or when s is a terminal state."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.038, 0.403, 0.577, 0.449], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "What about if we want to be flexible about depth limit?"}]}, {"type": "image", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.04, 0.483, 0.219, 0.754], "content": [{"type": "image_body", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.04, 0.483, 0.219, 0.754], "content": ""}, {"type": "image_footnote", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.079, 0.764, 0.158, 0.787], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "(a) White to move"}]}]}, {"type": "image", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.255, 0.482, 0.434, 0.784], "content": [{"type": "image_body", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.255, 0.482, 0.434, 0.784], "content": ""}, {"type": "image_footnote", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.036, 0.799, 0.41, 0.863], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Two chess positions that differ only in the position of the rook at lower right. In (a), Black has an advantage of a knight and two pawns, which should be enough to win the game. In (b), White will capture the queen, giving it an advantage that should be strong enough to win."}]}]}, {"type": "image", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.63, 0.311, 1.0, 0.904], "content": [{"type": "image_body", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.63, 0.311, 1.0, 0.904], "content": ""}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.054, 0.924, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.109, 0.938, 0.285, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 7, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.039, 0.112, 0.657, 0.177], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adversarial Search - Cutoff Search"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.259, 0.931, 0.303], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Maybe only cut off when state is quiescent: No pending move that would drastically change evaluation"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.038, 0.355, 0.736, 0.398], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "How can we know if a state is quiescent or not? Have to look a little bit deeper..."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.039, 0.45, 0.344, 0.493], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "How much deeper? 1 ply? 2 plies?"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.054, 0.924, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.108, 0.938, 0.286, 0.966], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 8, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.039, 0.112, 0.828, 0.179], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adversarial Search - Cutoff Search - Horizon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.244, 0.4, 0.347], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Black bishop on a2 will be captured, eventually"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.038, 0.407, 0.413, 0.565], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "It isn't about to be captured, but there is no escape for it, eventually white's king can go to c1, then b2, then a2."}]}, {"type": "chart", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.564, 0.302, 0.898, 0.9], "content": [{"type": "chart_body", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.564, 0.302, 0.898, 0.9], "content": ""}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.055, 0.924, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.109, 0.938, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 9, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.039, 0.112, 0.828, 0.179], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adversarial Search - Cutoff Search - Horizon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.244, 0.4, 0.347], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Black bishop on a2 will be captured, eventually"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.038, 0.406, 0.413, 0.565], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "It isn't about to be captured, but there is no escape for it, eventually white's king can go to c1, then b2, then a2."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.04, 0.625, 0.402, 0.674], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This is 6 ply away from current state"}]}, {"type": "chart", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.563, 0.301, 0.898, 0.9], "content": [{"type": "chart_body", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.563, 0.301, 0.898, 0.9], "content": ""}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.054, 0.923, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.109, 0.938, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 10, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.039, 0.112, 0.828, 0.179], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adversarial Search - Cutoff Search - Horizon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.037, 0.244, 0.463, 0.348], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Suppose that we are playing as black, and our search cutoff is 6 ply"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.038, 0.406, 0.434, 0.565], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Most of our action choices will result in white moving the king to go capture the bishop, and our search will see that"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.037, 0.625, 0.46, 0.78], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "But there is one move where we can force the king to move away from the bishop... what is it?"}]}, {"type": "chart", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.564, 0.301, 0.898, 0.9], "content": [{"type": "chart_body", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.564, 0.301, 0.898, 0.9], "content": ""}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.054, 0.923, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.108, 0.937, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 11, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.039, 0.112, 0.828, 0.179], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adversarial Search - Cutoff Search - Horizon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.244, 0.286, 0.291], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "e3+ (Pawn to e3, check)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.038, 0.351, 0.451, 0.511], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "White's response will be to capture the pawn with the king, otherwise its rook will be captured. Does this save the bishop?"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.037, 0.57, 0.443, 0.675], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "How far away is the bishop capture after white's king takes the pawn on e3?"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.039, 0.733, 0.322, 0.783], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "8 ply! (Past our search limit)"}]}, {"type": "chart", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.564, 0.302, 0.898, 0.9], "content": [{"type": "chart_body", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.564, 0.302, 0.898, 0.9], "content": ""}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.054, 0.923, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.108, 0.937, 0.286, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 12, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.039, 0.112, 0.828, 0.179], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adversarial Search - Cutoff Search - Horizon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.037, 0.244, 0.447, 0.508], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Horizon effect: Even though a bad state is inevitable, it seems like that outcome can be avoided by taking other moves, pushing the bad outcome “over the horizon”"}]}, {"type": "chart", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.564, 0.301, 0.897, 0.9], "content": [{"type": "chart_body", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.564, 0.301, 0.897, 0.9], "content": ""}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.055, 0.924, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.109, 0.938, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 13, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.039, 0.112, 0.657, 0.178], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adversarial Search - Cutoff Search"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.243, 0.952, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Even if we have a good way to extend our depth limit, we still have a big thing to think about: How do we build a “good” eval function?"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.038, 0.384, 0.955, 0.502], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Chess example (i.e. pawns = 1, bishops/knights = 3, rooks = 5, queens = 8) is very simplistic\nOther ideas?"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.054, 0.924, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.109, 0.938, 0.286, 0.966], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 14, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.039, 0.111, 0.856, 0.18], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adversarial Search - Monte Carlo Tree Search"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.244, 0.708, 0.292], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Eval functions are hard! Maybe we can come up with a better idea?"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.04, 0.352, 0.36, 0.398], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To estimate the value of a state:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.038, 0.406, 0.897, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Simulate a number of playouts from that state, then calculate average utility over those playouts"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.038, 0.57, 0.622, 0.62], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "How do we determine what moves to take in our playouts?"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.037, 0.678, 0.899, 0.784], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Playout Policy: Some (hopefully simple) calculation that will bias our playouts towards taking “better” moves. Still random, but biased randomness."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.038, 0.842, 0.866, 0.891], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Maybe we can focus computational resources on certain moves that “seem” better?"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.054, 0.924, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.108, 0.938, 0.286, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 15, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.041, 0.113, 0.486, 0.176], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Monte Carlo Tree Search"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.244, 0.672, 0.292], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Maintain a search tree, and grow it according to following steps:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.052, 0.316, 0.188, 0.358], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Selection"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.051, 0.457, 0.201, 0.503], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "- Expansion"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.052, 0.599, 0.2, 0.644], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Simulation"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.052, 0.742, 0.27, 0.788], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Back-propagation"}]}, {"type": "image", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.629, 0.311, 0.999, 0.904], "content": [{"type": "image_body", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.629, 0.311, 0.999, 0.904], "content": ""}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.054, 0.923, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.109, 0.938, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 16, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.041, 0.113, 0.486, 0.176], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Monte Carlo Tree Search"}], "level": 2}, {"type