tent": "Monte Carlo Tree Search"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.218, 0.375, 0.259], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "How do we choose a selection policy?"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.038, 0.36, 0.199, 0.404], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Book Suggestion:"}]}, {"type": "equation", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.267, 0.343, 0.617, 0.434], "content": "U C B 1 (n) = \\frac {U (n)}{N (n)} + C \\times \\sqrt {\\frac {\\log N (\\mathrm{PARENT} (n))}{N (n)}}"}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.038, 0.547, 0.359, 0.588], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Upper Confidence Bound for node n"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.04, 0.594, 0.454, 0.636], "content": [{"type": "equation_inline", "content": "U(n)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  - Total utility of all playouts through node n"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.039, 0.643, 0.409, 0.684], "content": [{"type": "equation_inline", "content": "N(n)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  - Number of playouts through node n"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.04, 0.69, 0.778, 0.732], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "C - Constant that balances exploration and exploitation, usually 1.414... (for reasons)"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.054, 0.923, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.108, 0.938, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 35, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.041, 0.112, 0.824, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Monte Carlo Tree Search - Very Pseudocode"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "code", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.04, 0.25, 0.428, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "code_body", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.04, 0.25, 0.428, 0.581], "content": "def monte_carlo_tree_search(state):\n    tree = Node(state)\n    while is_time_remaining():\n        leaf = Select(tree)\n        child = Expand(leaf)\n        result = Simulate(child)\n        BackPropagate(result, child)"}], "sub_type": "code", "guess_lang": "python"}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.083, 0.586, 0.89, 0.63], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "return the move in Actions(state) whose node has highest number of playouts"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.179, 0.699, 0.854, 0.828], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Intuition: Our policies should prefer to explore actions that are good for us and bad for our opponent. Therefore, the action that we’ve explored the most is our best choice!"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.055, 0.924, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.109, 0.938, 0.286, 0.966], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 36, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.04, 0.112, 0.486, 0.178], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Monte Carlo Tree Search"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.037, 0.218, 0.953, 0.316], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Versions of Monte Carlo Tree Search, combined with advanced neural networks, are used in top game-playing agents (AlphaGo, AlphaZero, LeelaChessZero)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.038, 0.36, 0.669, 0.41], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Good approach when evaluation functions aren't easy to create"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.054, 0.924, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.108, 0.938, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 37, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.041, 0.113, 0.67, 0.182], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Monte Carlo Tree Search - Example"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.218, 0.384, 0.345], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Comment: It seems like these numbers don't add up correctly. Is there something wrong with the tree?"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.04, 0.385, 0.172, 0.421], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A few caveats:"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.048, 0.426, 0.377, 0.547], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1. The initialization is handled as a special case, with an initial root that has 0/0"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.046, 0.55, 0.387, 0.798], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "2. Selection and expansion aren't as simple as described. Either (a) selection can choose non-leaf nodes, or (b) expansion adds all children of a node, creating a playout from only one"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.038, 0.799, 0.382, 0.884], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "So yes, this tree couldn't be created by my original algorithm description"}]}, {"type": "image", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.396, 0.2, 1.0, 0.904], "content": [{"type": "image_body", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.396, 0.2, 1.0, 0.904], "content": ""}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.054, 0.924, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.109, 0.938, 0.285, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 38, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.04, 0.113, 0.712, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stochastic (Non-Deterministic) Games"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.038, 0.218, 0.585, 0.26], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Many games include elements of chance (i.e. dice, cards, etc.)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.037, 0.313, 0.935, 0.404], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In dice-rolling games, often a player will roll dice, then get to act, then opponent will roll dice, then get to act, etc. The results of the dice are what determine possible actions for each player."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.037, 0.456, 0.959, 0.547], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "So, when an agent is able to act, the agent knows what the possible actions it could take are, but does not know what the opponent's dice roll will be."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.037, 0.599, 0.905, 0.691], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If we know probability of each outcome, then we should be able to calculate an expected value of a position. The average over all possible outcomes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.039, 0.742, 0.902, 0.785], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To evaluate a node, we cannot use a minimax value, but we will instead use expectiminimax value"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.054, 0.924, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.108, 0.938, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 39, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.04, 0.111, 0.712, 0.186], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stochastic (Non-Deterministic) Games"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "code", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.04, 0.215, 0.999, 0.904], "content": [{"type": "code_body", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.04, 0.215, 0.999, 0.904], "content": "Minimax(s) =\n  Utility(s, Max)                  if Is-Terminal(s)\n  max_a Minimax(Result(s,a))          if To-Move(s) == Max\n  min_a Minimax(Result(s,a))          if To-Move(s) == Min\n\nExpectiminimax(s) =\n  Utility(s, Max)                 if Is-Terminal(s)\n  max_a Expectiminimax(Result(s,a))   if To-Move(s) == Max\n  min_a Expectiminimax(Result(s,a))   if To-Move(s) == Min\n  Σ_r P(r) Expectiminimax(Result(s,a)) if To-Move(s) == Chance"}], "sub_type": "code", "guess_lang": "scala"}, {"type": "footer", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.054, 0.923, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.108, 0.938, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 40, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.04, 0.111, 0.712, 0.186], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stochastic (Non-Deterministic) Games"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "code", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.04, 0.215, 0.999, 0.904], "content": [{"type": "code_body", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.04, 0.215, 0.999, 0.904], "content": "Minimax(s) =\n  Utility(s, Max)                  if Is-Terminal(s)\n  max_a Minimax(Result(s,a))          if To-Move(s) == Max\n  min_a Minimax(Result(s,a))          if To-Move(s) == Min\n\nExpectiminimax(s) =\n  Utility(s, Max)                 if Is-Terminal(s)\n  max_a Expectiminimax(Result(s,a))   if To-Move(s) == Max\n  min_a Expectiminimax(Result(s,a))   if To-Move(s) == Min\n  Σ_r P(r) Expectiminimax(Result(s,a)) if To-Move(s) == Chance"}], "sub_type": "code", "guess_lang": "scala"}, {"type": "footer", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.054, 0.923, 0.107, 0.98], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "M"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.108, 0.938, 0.286, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 41, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.04, 0.111, 0.713, 0.186], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stochastic (Non-Deterministic) Games"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.058, 0.294, 0.182, 0.34], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Chance node"}]}, {"type": "image", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.23, 0.404, 0.289, 0.619], "content": [{"type": "image_body", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.23, 0.404, 0.289, 0.619], "content": ""}]}, {"type": "image", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.323, 0.402, 0.379, 0.615], "content": [{"type": "image_body", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.323, 0.402, 0.379, 0.615], "con